\section{Related Work}

\paragraph{Safe Robot Learning.}
Inference-time VLA safety methods include SDF-guided denoising \citep{song2026omniguide}, CBF-based trajectory projection \citep{hu2025aegis}, and CBF-embedded diffusion \citep{xiao2025safediffuser}. These approaches offer robustness to novel obstacles through real-time geometric checks, but add latency, require runtime scene geometry acquisition, and risk pushing corrected actions into out-of-distribution states. Training-time approaches such as SafeVLA \citep{zhang2025safevla} reduce safety cost via constrained policy optimization \citep{zhao2024scpo} but lack geometric grounding for precise spatial collision reasoning. \ours{} resolves this tension by internalizing SDF collision geometry into VLA weights during training, producing safe actions with zero inference overhead.

\paragraph{Vision-Language-Action Models.}
$\pi_0$ \citep{black2024pi0} introduced a flow-matching VLA built on PaliGemma, and $\pi_{0.5}$ \citep{black2025pi05} extended it to open-world generalization with open-source weights via the openpi codebase. Recent work has explored geometric priors: GLaD \citep{guo2025glad} distills 3D geometric features into VLA hidden states, achieving 94.1\% success on LIBERO, but targets general spatial understanding rather than collision safety. \ours{} builds on $\pi_{0.5}$ and extends geometric internalization specifically to collision awareness.

\paragraph{SDF in Robotics and Guidance Distillation.}
SDF representations have been adopted in manipulation planning \citep{chen2026cssdf,weng2023ngdf}, and several VLA works use a ``train-with-geometry, infer-without'' paradigm for general spatial accuracy \citep{liu2025occvla,li2025spatial,qian2025geopredict}. Separately, \citet{meng2023distillation} showed that classifier-free guidance can be distilled into diffusion model weights. \ours{} transfers both ideas to VLA safety: we internalize configuration-space SDF into flow-matching velocity fields through an auxiliary head discarded at inference, combining collision-specific geometric supervision with full weight internalization.


