\subsection*{Limitations}

\paragraph{Single benchmark and backbone.} All experiments were conducted on LIBERO/SafeLIBERO with $\pi_{0.5}$. Validating on additional benchmarks (ManiSkill, RoboCasa) and VLA architectures (Octo, RT-2) would strengthen generality claims.

\paragraph{Known geometry assumption.} Ground-truth SDF labels require analytical scene geometry (MuJoCo). Real-world deployment will need neural SDF estimation from depth or point clouds, and the effect of label noise on collision shaping remains uncharacterized.

\paragraph{Simulation only.} All results are simulated; a real-robot validation is needed to confirm that internalized collision awareness survives the sim-to-real gap.

